## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle external dependency fragility, multi-tenant isolation, and production risk management. The question evaluates end-to-end instrumentation, resilience patterns, and practical operational procedures rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry
- Retry budgets with exponential backoff and jitter
- Circuit breakers with configurable thresholds and recovery
- Backpressure through token bucket rate limiting
- Idempotent retries with deduplication keys
- Progressive canary rollouts with automated rollback
- Incident runbooks and alerting thresholds
- SLO/SLI definition and percentile-based monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Circuit breaker around identity provider
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold = 5, timeout = 3000) {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  async execute(operation) {
    if (this.state === 'OPEN') {
      if (Date.now() - this.lastFailure > this.timeout) {
        this.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      } else {
        throw new Error('Circuit breaker is OPEN');
      }
    }

    try {
      const result = await operation();
      this.onSuccess();
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      this.onFailure();
      throw error;
    }
  }

  onSuccess() {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  onFailure() {
    this.failureCount++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failureCount >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
    }
  }
}
```

